issue:
Bug. If a model wraps JSON in an untagged fence (   with no json), split("json")[-1] returns the whole reply and .split("")[0] returns the text *before* the first fence (the chat preamble, or ""), so json.loads fails and the reply is counted unparseable. Verified: parse('Here it is:

{"a":1}
') → None; parse('
{"a":1}
') → None. The Line-by-line claims fence stripping "absorbs the two most common formatting habits".
